narrator: Anna is three minutes early again. You found a timestamp on the post-it she left on your desk rearrangement.
narrator: This one has four colour categories of highlights.
join anna (Neutral) center
anna: "I've been thinking about what we discussed."
player: "So have I."
narrator: She gives you a sharp look. Then, softer:
anna: "I had a weird dream."
narrator: She says it lightly, but she's already uncapping and recapping her pen.
player: "Tell me."
anna: "It's — I mean, it's just a dream. But it kept recurring and I figured you'd probably want to know."
player: "Probably, yes."
anna: "So there's a project at work — hypothetically. And my boss is directing it very specifically. Like, there's a rubric. For everything. Weighted scoring criteria for every deliverable."
narrator: A beat.
anna: "And in the dream, that's... fine. Actually."
narrator: She stops.
player: "Just fine?"
narrator: A very careful recalibration behind her eyes.
anna: "I kept a log of the recurring elements. In case it's useful."
narrator: She opens her phone. It's a spreadsheet. The dream journal has a pivot table.
[photo_opportunity id="anna_spreadsheet" patient="anna" title="The Spreadsheet Confession" description="A color-coded dream journal with emotional-valence columns and conditional formatting." portrait="res://assets/photos/anna/spreadsheet.png"]
if {flags.last_photo_success}:
	narrator: The expression when she shows you the screen — half sheepish, half defiant — is a useful data point.
	do PatientManager.add_therapy("anna", 15)
player: "What were you feeling in the dream?"
anna: "Calm."
narrator: Then:
anna: "Focused."
player: "Mmm."
anna: "It's just — work stress manifests in dreams. I looked it up."
player: "It does, yes."
narrator: She's recapping the pen faster now.
[stat_check stat="perception"]
if {check_result}:
	narrator: There's a tell. The pen speed correlates with the gap between what she's saying and what she means.
	- Anna. You weren't anxious in the dream. You wanted the rubric. | [if {stats.intellect} >= 2] [else="disable"]
		narrator: A long silence.
		anna: "I don't—"
		player: "The dream wasn't a stress dream. It was a wish."
		narrator: She puts the pen down. Stares at it.
		anna: "That's a very specific interpretation."
		player: "Is it wrong?"
		narrator: No answer. Which is an answer.
		set {flags.anna_named_fixation_s2} = true
		do PatientManager.add_therapy("anna", 20)
		[add_note patient="anna" note="Session 2 — Named the fixation directly: craves structured direction, not autonomy. She didn't deny it."]
	- Tell me more about what 'calm' felt like.
		anna: "Like everything was in its place."
		player: "Everything, or you?"
		narrator: A flicker. Then:
		anna: "Anyway, the sleep has actually been better."
		do PatientManager.add_therapy("anna", 20)
else:
	- Dreams about work are usually just processing stress. That sounds healthy.
		anna: "Right. Yes. That's what I thought."
		narrator: Relief that's almost desperate.
		do PatientManager.add_therapy("anna", -3)
	- Tell me more about the rubric itself.
		anna: "It's — it's just a rubric."
		narrator: You wait.
		anna: "It had color coding. By priority tier."
		player: "That sounds like something you'd design."
		anna: "It sounds like something any rational person would design."
		do PatientManager.add_therapy("anna", 2)
player: "Before we close — how's the sleep now?"
anna: "Four AM is now four-thirty."
narrator: A beat.
anna: "Progress."
player: "Progress."
[add_note patient="anna" note="Session 2 — Described recurring dream involving explicit task frameworks and structured direction. Deflection noted."]
leave anna
do PatientManager.mark_session_done("anna")
jump between_patients/
